      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>To provide humanitarian relief to refugees people experiencing poverty and those in need in Mexico and the County of San Diego USA</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>As-Sabil Shelter-Tijuana Mexico. In our second year we continued our shelter in Tijuana. We admitted approximately 100 refugees. We provided them with meals a place to sleep and medical and dental checkups in the U.S. Besides having a Shelter for Refugees we provide them with a full-time Imam minister a prayer for men and women and provide food for underserved locals. Finally we empower refugee programs by teaching them English skills and providing school transportation for refugee families with school-aged children. s an integral part of refugees approved asylum and humanitarian parole transition to their new home in America we work with refugees in Mexico awaiting their asylum and humanitarian parole applications to be processed and their legal admission to the US. Finally we provide transportation to the U.S. and a hotel room in San Diego CA for legally admitted refugees. We serve approximately 100 refugees a month and engage in our Shelter activities.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>0</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>In Vera Cruz Leon and Chiapas during Ramadan we break our fast at sunset with a meal. Besides feeding the refugees at the shelter and providing Islamic Holidays Food Distribution during our traditional holidays Ramadan and Hajj we expanded our food distribution to locals in Tijuana and to the poor in Vera Cruz Leon and Chiapas. We collect donations from the Muslim communities throughout the county of San Diego and use those funds to purchase meals for 30 days for the needy in the various communities in Mexico. Next we expanded our food distribution to the poor in Vera Cruz Leon and Chiapas during the Hajj season. In honor of Abrahams Islamic practice of sacrificing a livestock animal such as a cow or goat at Eid ul-Adha the meat slaughtered is called a Qurbani. We distributed this Qurbani to the poor in Tijuana Vera Cruz and Leon.also feed the</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>0</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>0</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Humanitarian Relief in San Diego. We provide food blankets clothing and out-of-pocket medical costs for caregivers to those in need in the county.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
